# nr-tui-termtext-ansi-wrap: wiring for mixdog-termtext (lead applies, then deletes this file)

## 1. native/core/Cargo.lock
Anchor: `[[package]]` `name = "mixdog-termtext"`. Its `dependencies` list gains one entry, in sorted place, so the list is
    "mixdog-js",
    "serde_json",
    "unicode-normalization",
    "unicode-segmentation",
(The crate's own Cargo.toml already has the line `unicode-normalization = { workspace = true }`, a workspace dependency that
exists: `unicode-normalization = "0.1"` in native/core/Cargo.toml, locked at 0.1.26. No new external crate, no new
workspace member, no change to the workspace Cargo.toml. wrap-ansi normalises text to NFC before wrapping, which is what
the dependency is for.)

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Nothing from this task: the termtext entry of the width wire (nr-tui-termtext-width.wire, item 3) still applies once.

## 3. Nothing else
No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING change, no registration, no pending-rows fragment.

## Interfaces added (for the tasks that consume them)
All in crate mixdog-termtext, modules public (lib.rs lists them; its doc line "declare the interfaces the ANSI-aware wrapping
task fills in" is stale now and may be reworded by whoever next edits lib.rs):
- ansi: AnsiToken{Text, Escape}, tokenize (lossless); InkToken/InkTokenKind, tokenize_ink, has_ansi_control_characters
  (ink/build/ansi-tokenizer.js); AnsiCode, StyledToken{Ansi, Control, Char}, StyledChar, tokenize_styled(text, end_char),
  end_code_of, link_start_code, reduce_ansi_codes(_incremental), undo_ansi_codes, diff_ansi_codes, ansi_codes_to_string,
  styled_chars_from_tokens, styled_chars_to_string (@alcalzone/ansi-tokenize).
- wrap: WrapOptions, WrapMode (now also Hash), wrap_ansi; wrap_text / wrap_text_with(.., wide) (Ink wrapText, cached /
  policy as argument); measure_text / measure_text_with and TextSize; sanitize_ansi; slice_text_by_display_width(_with);
  wrap_lines, hard_wrap_ansi_lines / hard_wrap_ansi_lines_with (ansi-line-wrap.mjs).
- slice: slice_ansi(text, start, end) (slice-ansi 9.0.0).
- truncate: TruncatePosition, TruncateOptions{position, space, prefer_truncation_on_space, truncation_character},
  truncate / truncate_with (cli-truncate 6.0.0).
- spans: SgrColor, SgrStyle, SgrLink, StyledRun{text, style, link}, StyledLine, parse_sgr, xterm256_rgb (AnsiText.jsx parser;
  colours stay SGR indexes, the renderer maps an index below 16 to its theme colour and 16 and up with xterm256_rgb).

## Verify commands that need the lead
cargo test --offline -p mixdog-termtext; cargo clippy --offline -p mixdog-termtext --all-targets -- -D warnings;
node native/core/crates/mixdog-termtext/tests/recorders/record-wrap.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --check native/core/crates/mixdog-termtext/tests/goldens/wrap.json
